# Cloudflare Pages — ترويسات HTTP
# Advisory / Agricultural Advisor
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file verbatim and serves the headers below.
# Format: "<path pattern>" then indented "Name: value" lines. Blank lines separate blocks.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy here is the SAME policy the page already declares
# in its <meta http-equiv>. The most restrictive of the two applies, so this
# header tightens nothing and breaks nothing: it exists so the policy is
# enforced even before the document body is parsed. (Framing defense stays
# X-Frame-Options: DENY — CSP cannot carry frame-ancestors from <meta>, and
# the single-source-of-truth guard in tests/headers-injection.test.mjs keeps
# header == meta on purpose.)
# HSTS is safe and correct: the site is HTTPS-only on its own domain.
#
# NOTE ON DIRECTORIES: Cloudflare Pages serves _headers as a static asset; that is
# intentional. It contains no secrets — only public policy.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# The service worker must never be cached, or a stale worker outlives a release.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# The reference data is content-addressed by the app's own checksums; the browser
# must not keep a stale copy of it.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
